          "unit_id": "looking_back",
          "title": "Home",
          "description": "Mira atrás y cuenta tu historia: past perfect continuous, would y used to. Además, la pasiva en todas sus formas para contar una historia: had been given, might have been lost, having been told.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "looking_back_lesson",
              "title": "Narrative tenses: had been doing, would and used to",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Home",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Three years ago, I arrived on Clifton Road with a suitcase, a Spanish fan and very little English."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I had been studying English for months, but I couldn't understand a word the bus driver said."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Mrs Green, who's here tonight, gave me a key and told me I'd be fine. She was right."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "In those first weeks, I would get lost every Saturday, and Daniel would give me directions. I used to think \"craic\" was a kind of bread."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Sam lent me his grandmother's lamp and an umbrella, which the wind destroyed a month later."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Priya taught me that tea solves almost everything, and Ollie proved that good soup solves the rest."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "And Helen, who had been running Harbour Studio for twenty years, gave a nervous Spanish designer her first real chance."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Little did I know that this city would become my home. Thank you, Bristol."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "That was perfect. Come outside for a minute. I've been waiting all night to ask you something."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Daniel… what's in your hand?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Daniel",
                        "text": "Lucía Martín, will you marry me?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Yes! Of course I will!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Javi",
                        "text": "I knew it! I told Mum two years ago!"
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "October. Green Door Design has just won the Bristol Business Award. Everyone is there: Daniel, Priya, Sam, Ollie, Mrs Green, Helen, and Javi, who has flown in from Dublin. Lucía walks up to the stage."
                  }
                },
