                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "narrative_tenses",
                    "title": "Narrative tenses: had been doing, would and used to",
                    "explanation": "Para contar una historia con matices:\n- past perfect continuous («had been» + «-ing»): una actividad que duraba hasta un momento del pasado: «I had been studying English for months, but I couldn't understand the bus driver.»\n- «would» + verbo: acciones repetidas en el pasado, típico de la narración nostálgica. Solo sirve para acciones, no para estados: «I would get lost every Saturday.»\n- «used to» + verbo: hábitos y también estados del pasado: «I used to think 'craic' was a kind of bread.»\n- past perfect simple: acción terminada antes de otra.\n- past simple: los hechos principales.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Forma",
                        "Uso",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "had been + -ing",
                          "actividad que duraba hasta un momento del pasado",
                          "I had been studying English for months."
                        ],
                        [
                          "would + verbo",
                          "acción repetida en el pasado (no estados)",
                          "I would get lost every Saturday."
                        ],
                        [
                          "used to + verbo",
                          "hábitos y estados del pasado",
                          "I used to think 'craic' was a kind of bread."
                        ],
                        [
                          "had + participio",
                          "acción terminada antes",
                          "Helen had already given me a chance."
                        ],
                        [
                          "past simple",
                          "hechos principales",
                          "I arrived on Clifton Road with a suitcase."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I had been studying English for months, but I couldn't understand a word the bus driver said.",
                      "In those first weeks, I would get lost every Saturday, and Daniel would give me directions.",
                      "I used to think \"craic\" was a kind of bread.",
                      "Little did I know that this city would become my home."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "passive_all",
                    "title": "The passive in all its forms",
                    "explanation": "A nivel C1 la pasiva aparece en cualquier tiempo y con modales, sobre todo en narraciones y textos formales:\n- Past perfect: «I had been given a key before I arrived.»\n- Future perfect: «By the time we get there, all the seats will have been taken.»\n- Modal perfect: «The umbrella might have been destroyed by the wind.», «It can't have been stolen.»\n- Continua: «I felt I was being watched.»\n- Participio perfecto («having been» + participio): «Having been told it rained a lot, I bought an umbrella.»\n- Infinitivo y gerundio: «She hates being interrupted.», «He's going to be given an award.»\n\nEl agente con «by» solo se añade si aporta información:\n- «Harbour Studio was founded by Helen twenty years ago.»",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Forma",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Past perfect",
                          "She had been offered a job in Bristol."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Future perfect",
                          "The office will have been painted by Monday."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Modal perfect",
                          "The letter might have been lost."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Continua",
                          "I thought I was being followed."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Having been + participio",
                          "Having been told about the rain, I packed an umbrella."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Gerundio",
                          "Nobody likes being ignored."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I had been offered the job before I had even seen Bristol.",
                      "Having been warned about the weather, I packed three jumpers.",
                      "The black umbrella might have been destroyed by the wind, but the red one survived.",
                      "By next year, the studio will have been open for two years."
                    ]
                  }
                },
